From 9ff36ef02a212d81d941732677309bde714b0e5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phaer <hello@phaer.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:00:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] imds: import SSH keys provided as a JSON array

Some IMDS services only provide the SSH keys of an instance as one JSON
array of strings. Hetzner Cloud does that at /metadata/public-keys, and
has no path that returns a single key in plain text, so systemd-imds
currently cannot import any of its keys.

Add a new well-known key "ssh-key-json" (IMDS_KEY_SSH_KEY_JSON= in hwdb,
systemd.imds.key.ssh_key_json= on the kernel command line, the
imds.key_ssh_key_json credential). "systemd-imds --import" parses it and
writes each key as one line of the ssh.authorized_keys.root credential,
after the keys of "ssh-key" if both are set. An entry which is not a
string, or which contains control characters (and so could turn into
more than one authorized_keys line), is skipped with a warning, and the
other keys are still imported.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (claude-opus-5-5)
